The driver provides support for the Philips/NXP TEA5767 FM stereo
radio.  The can tune in the range 87.5 - 108.0 MHz, perform hard‐
ware  signal search and supports mono/stereo toggling.  The flags
control the FM Band, XTAL, and PLL values as follows: Sets the FM
Band to Japan.  Sets the PLL bit.  Sets the XTAL bit.  Force  en‐
ables  hardware  search support.  Many popular TEA5767 evaluation
boards feature low quality 32.768kHz crystals.  The inaccuracy of
these crystals may often lead  to  malfunction  of  the  hardware
search function.  Therefore, the driver tries to detect the crys‐
tal  quality  during  attachment.  If the crystal of insufficient
accuracy was detected, the hardware search function is  disabled.
It can be forcefully re‐enabled by setting the 0x08 flag.
